  "note": "The Hollins household at 2 Clinton Terrace on the 1891 return, transcribed by A. Hagues. None of the seven was in the record, and 2 Clinton Terrace (#72) held no census household at all. Wright's Directory of Nottingham agrees on the house: 1894-95 lists Claude Hollins, of W. Hollins & Co., at 129 Derby Road, which is 2 Clinton Terrace's Derby Road number. By 1898-99 he is at 7 Cavendish Crescent North, a director of W. Hollins & Co. Ltd. William A. Hollins, a mixture yarn spinner at 5 Tattershall Drive in 1921, is likely family but is not linked here, because nothing on this return shows it. Ages are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way.",
